{"id": "1becdb48-a662-44a0-a8d2-f4547e6131a1", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:37:27.467050", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-25T00:36\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "2ef1a25d-298a-4344-bed0-736248376cac", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:37:27.469451", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1becdb48-a662-44a0-a8d2-f4547e6131a1", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Thanks. Before we commit to the full experiment design, please do a scoped inspection pass and report back:\\n\\n1) Input/repo inspection: Check /workspace for anything relevant (OPRO artifacts such as discovered instruction strings, optimization trajectories, BBH task lists/data, prior evaluation scripts or result logs). Report what actually exists versus what is absent. Do not run the full experiment; a light directory listing and quick file peeks are enough. Note any package/dataset availability constraints (e.g., whether BBH data or an LLM API would even be reachable in this offline environment).\\n\\n2) Proposed approach outline: Sketch, at a high level, how you would design a design-only experiment answering whether OPRO-optimized instructions beat the two baselines (\\\"Let's think step by step.\\\" and empty prompt) on BBH. Indicate the comparison structure you are considering (task selection across BBH's ~23 tasks, model(s) and decoding settings, prompt/answer-extraction protocol, metrics, and how you would handle variance and multiple comparisons).\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties: List the assumptions your design would rest on that are NOT confirmed by the source materials, for example: which OPRO paper settings (which model, which BBH subset vs full suite, temperature, answer extraction regex), whether we assume access to the original OPRO-discovered instructions or must treat them as given inputs, and any budget assumptions. Flag any place where the OPRO paper's own evaluation protocol (e.g., few-shot vs zero-shot cot mode, which tasks were optimized vs held out) must be respected for a fair comparison.\\n\\nKeep this to inspection + approach sketch only; I will review and then we will proceed to the full design.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions ('Let's think step by step.' and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
