used; the other becomes secondary. The scope is recorded in the pre-registration as **unconfirmed**, never as fact. If neither can be verified, the primary analysis is declared ambiguous and both arms are reported jointly \\u2014 this branch is stated up front, not resolved silently.\\n- **P2 \\u2014 BBH data** (23 tasks, official BIG-Bench-Hard collection).\\n- **P3 \\u2014 Grader code**: BIG-Bench-Hard `cot/`-directory-style extra-grades (pinned commit; see \\u00a76).\\n\\n## 3. Condition table (fully crossed: condition \\u00d7 task \\u00d7 model)\\n| ID | Instruction text | Assembly (byte-level, validated in t01) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| C_OPRO_task | per-task I_t (input P1) | `I_t + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + question` |\\n| C_OPRO_global | global I (input P1) | `I + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + question` |\\n| C_COT | `Let's think step by step.` | `\\\"Let's think step by step.\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + question` |\\n| C_EMPTY | (none) | `question` **verbatim** \\u2014 no leading separator, no added whitespace |\\n\\nRules pinned: separator is exactly two `\\\\n`; UTF-8; no chat wrappers in the primary replication arm (base completion-style prompts to mirror the paper's zero-shot \\\"simple\\\" setup); question text unmodified from the BBH jsonl. A chat-template arm for API models is a labeled robustness arm only, applied to **all** conditions equally.\\n\\n## 4. Splits \\u2014 committed primary framing (branch made explicit, per researcher directive)\\n- **Primary framing (decision):** Attempt reconstruction of the paper's train/dev/test split (procedure described in the paper; seed recoverable from released optimization code/config if obtainable). **If and only if the exact split is byte-reproducible**, the primary endpoint is leakage-free evaluation on those frozen test splits (\\\"test-split comparison\\\").\\n- **Declared fallback:** If the seed/split cannot be recovered (the likely case, given it is unverifiable from materials available here), the study is **explicitly designated a \\\"fresh-split\\\" comparison**: we construct our own deterministic frozen split (250 test items per task; hash-based item ordering by item text SHA-256; documented split script committed before any generation). Because OPRO instructions were tuned on some portion of items that may fall in our test split, **claim strength is downgraded to \\\"performance on a fresh split that may contain items the optimizer saw\\\"**, and this appears verbatim in a dedicated Threats-to-Validity section (\\u00a79, T1).\\n- **Secondary diagnostic arm (arm D):** evaluate the OPRO arm additionally on the *train* split(s) it was optimized on (or, under fresh-split fallback, on the largest recoverable proxy) to quantify the **optimization-overfit gap** = (train-split accuracy \\u2212 test-split accuracy) per task, and its difference vs. baselines. This arm never contributes to the primary endpoint.\\n\\n## 5. Models and decoding\\n- **Reference model (primary):** instruction-tuned Flan-UL2 \\u2014 the model family central to the OPRO paper's BBH evaluation; comparing here best mirrors the source claim.\\n- **Replication models (secondary):** one API instruction model of the paper's era (GPT-3.5-turbo class) and one current open-weights instruction model, to test generalization of any instruction effect. All conclusions about the paper's claim rest on the reference model; others are robustness.\\n- **Decoding:** primary = temperature 0 (greedy / API default-deterministic), one generation per item per condition. Robustness arm = temperature 0.3, n=3 samples, all conditions, reported as mean-per-item; used only to show conclusions aren't decoding-fragile.\\n- max_tokens capped and identical per task family; truncation logged.\\n\\n## 6. Grading spec (pinned) and extraction audit\\n- **Grader:** official BIG-Bench-Hard grader functions (`cot/` subdirectory variants), pinned to a recorded git commit; **per-task grader map committed as a table before any run** (boolean/date/multistep-integer/etc. exact-match styles). `exact_str_match`-family handling with last-line answer extraction as designed and unit-tested in t02.\\n- **Substring sensitivity (validated in t02):** naive substring grading produced a demonstrable false positive (\\\"not yes\\\" matching \\\"yes\\\"); hence substring-prone tasks are graded only via the pinned task-specific extra-grades, and the substring demo is kept in the repo as rationale documentation.\\n- **Extraction-failure audit log:** every completion stored raw with (condition, model, task, item_id, split, decode_setting, extracted_answer, grade, extraction_failed flag). Primary analysis pre-specified as \\\"extraction failure = incorrect,\\\" with a sensitivity analysis excluding extraction failures. Audit compares failure rates **across conditions** \\u2014 differential failure rates are themselves a confound to report.\\n\\n## 7. Metrics and statistical analysis (pre-registered)\\n- **Primary metric:** macro-averaged per-task accuracy over the 23 test splits (mirrors the paper).\\n- **Primary contrasts (exactly two):** \\u03941 = macro-acc(C_OPRO) \\u2212 macro-acc(C_COT); \\u03942 = macro-acc(C_OPRO) \\u2212 macro-acc(C_EMPTY). Each tested with a **paired-by-item design** (identical items, models, decoding; only instruction varies) using a **task-stratified paired bootstrap over items** (\\u226510,000 resamples; machinery validated in t03) reporting 95% CIs; significance = CI excluding 0.\\n- **Secondary:** per-task \\u0394 with **Holm\\u2013Bonferroni across the 23 tests within each baseline family** (implementation cross-checked against a reference on 204 synthetic p-vectors incl. ties/boundaries, t03b); win-rate per task; simple-vs-hard task grouping; overfit-gap (arm D); extraction-failure deltas; robustness-arm agreement.\\n- **Multiplicity discipline:** only the two macro contrasts can support the headline claim; per-task results are always labeled exploratory/secondary.\\n\\n## 8. Power discussion (planning input, not a finding)\\nWith ~250 test items/task \\u00d7 23 tasks and pairing, the macro-difference CI half-width is driven mainly by between-task variance of the effect rather than item count; the design targets resolvability of macro differences on the order of ~1 percentage point under plausible within-task correlation assumptions (paper-reported baseline spreads in this range are the motivation for that target \\u2014 cited as planning rationale only). If pilot variance makes the omnibus underpowered, the pre-registered remedy is more bootstrap resamples and reporting the CI without a significance claim \\u2014 never post-hoc endpoint switching.\\n\\n## 9. Threats to validity\\n- **T1 \\u2014 Split leakage / fresh-split fallback (\\u00a74):** if the paper's split is unrecoverable, OPRO items leakage means the primary claim is explicitly weaker (\\\"fresh-split comparison\\\"); stated in all reporting.\\n- **T2 \\u2014 Instruction scope unresolved (P1):** per-task vs global designation is an input-dependent assumption; a wrong designation misattributes the paper's headline number \\u2014 mitigated by running both arms and reporting both regardless.\\n- **T3 \\u2014 Prompt-form drift:** exact instruction string, separator, and template can change results; byte-level templates (\\u00a73) and a golden-file test (t01 pattern) are committed.\\n- **T4 \\u2014 Grader sensitivity:** substring false positives demonstrated (t02); mitigated by pinned per-task extra-grades and raw-completion audit.\\n- **T5 \\u2014 Differential extraction failure across conditions** can masquerade as accuracy difference; handled by equal-treatment grading + audit + sensitivity analysis (\\u00a76).\\n- **T6 \\u2014 Model/version drift:** API model versions are pinned by name+date; open models pinned by weight hash.\\n- **T7 \\u2014 Single-seed instruction discovery:** OPRO instructions are one sample from an optimizer; the design can only test *these* instructions, not \\\"OPRO as a method.\\\" Stated as a scope limit.\\n\\n## 10. Feasibility (explicit)\\n**Nothing was executed; this is a protocol.** Actual execution requires, none of which exist here (verified offline: no network, no datasets/openai/anthropic packages, no caches): (a) BBH dataset files; (b) grader repo at pinned commit; (c) inference access \\u2014 Flan-UL2 weights (~70B-class, multi-GPU) and/or pinned API keys; (d) the OPRO instruction strings from paper appendix/trajectory logs; (e) results storage ~ a few GB. Budget at full scope \\u2248 23 tasks \\u00d7 250 items \\u00d7 4 conditions \\u00d7 1\\u20133 models \\u2248 23k\\u201369k generations (primary decoding only).\\n\\n## 11. Offline design-validation performed (NOT experimental results)\\nAll in `/workspace/design_validation/`, each header-labeled \\\"DESIGN VALIDATION ONLY\\\":\\n- **t01 template assembly:** PASS \\u2014 empty prompt = question verbatim (106 B), instruction arms = `instr + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + question`; assertions on separator bytes.\\n- **t02 grader logic:** PASS \\u2014 boolean/integer/date grading on synthetic items; substring-sensitivity false positive demonstrated, motivating the pinned grader spec.\\n- **t03/t03b statistics machinery:** PASS \\u2014 task-stratified paired bootstrap CI computes correctly; Holm implementation cross-checked against a stepwise-closure reference on 204 synthetic p-vectors (ties and boundaries). One buggy inline assertion in t03 was itself the failure, fixed and verified in t03b.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository/environment (from scoped inspection): /workspace contains only task.json; full-fs search found no OPRO/BBH artifacts; no network (DNS failure); datasets/openai/anthropic absent \\u2014 hence design-only. Researcher directives incorporated: committed split-leakage branch (test-split primary iff seed-reproducible, else declared fresh-split with stated claim downgrade, \\u00a74) plus train-split overfit diagnostic arm D; instruction scope as input-dependent parameter with both arms representable and labeled unresolved (\\u00a72/P1); byte-level templates, pinned per-task grader with substring-sensitivity note, paired bootstrap + single omnibus primary contrast + Holm secondaries, macro-averaged primary metric, temperature-0 primary with temperature-0.3 robustness arm, extraction-failure audit, feasibility section \\u2014 all present in \\u00a73\\u2013\\u00a710. Design-validation outputs (labeled synthetic-only): t01 \\\"TEMPLATE-ASSEMBLY CHECKS: PASS\\\"; t02 \\\"GRADER-LOGIC CHECKS: PASS\\\" + substring false-positive demo; t03 bootstrap CI machinery runs; t03b \\\"HOLM CROSS-CHECK vs REFERENCE: PASS (204 synthetic p-value vectors)\\\". No accuracy numbers on real data are reported anywhere; effect magnitudes appear only as planning rationale in \\u00a78.\", \"assumptions\": [\"UNRESOLVED SOURCE ASSUMPTION (input-dependent): OPRO instruction strings and their per-task-vs-global scope must be filled in from the paper appendix/trajectory logs at execution time; neither is confirmable from materials in this environment, and the design labels this as unconfirmed rather than fact.\", \"The OPRO paper's BBH evaluation mode is the zero-shot 'simple' setup; the primary arm therefore uses no few-shot exemplars for any condition.\", \"The COT baseline string is exactly \\\"Let's think step by step.\\\" as given in the task statement.\", \"The paper's split seed may be unrecoverable; the design does not assume recovery but branches on it (\\u00a74).\", \"Flan-UL2 (instruction-tuned) is the appropriate reference model for mirroring the paper's claim; other models are robustness only.\", \"Execution-time resources (BBH data, grader repo commit, model/API access) will be available in a future environment; none are available here \\u2014 this design task executed no experiment.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the paper's headline BBH configuration used per-task or global optimized instructions \\u2014 determines which OPRO arm is designated primary at execution time.\", \"Recoverability of the paper's exact train/dev/test split seed, which selects between the test-split and fresh-split primary framings (\\u00a74); the fresh-split branch weakens the headline claim by design.\", \"Whether substring-prone BBH tasks in the pinned grader commit fully mitigate the extraction sensitivity demonstrated in t02; execution should re-audit on real completions.\", \"Exact API model versions/pricing if the GPT-3.5-era replication arm is retained under budget constraints.\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
